  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Jakarta Metropolitan Police (Polda Metro Jaya) has been actively managing various legal and social initiatives across the capital region. In recent enforcement actions, authorities detained 11 individuals linked to human trafficking and the exploitation of children, identifying 16 victims affected by these crimes. Simultaneously, the force's Cyber Division initiated an inquiry into a social media personality identified as CAN following a formal complaint filed by an activist regarding alleged defamation. Beyond criminal investigations, the department has focused on public welfare and community outreach. This includes hosting health service events for workers in Bekasi and conducting educational programs at SMPN 72 Jakarta aimed at preventing student bullying. Additionally, the department is currently refining its internal procedures, including the selection of 116 personnel to serve as integrity-focused investigators.",
